  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p35.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking logarithms gives \\[ \\begin{gathered} x\\log a=q\\log c,\\\\ y\\log c=z\\log a. \\end{gathered} \\] Multiplying these equations and cancelling the nonzero logarithmic factors under the historical nondegenerate-base convention yields \\(xy=qz.\\)\n\nThus, the intended correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Take logarithms of both chains of equal powers",
        "From \\(x\\log a=q\\log c\\) and \\(y\\log c=z\\log a\\), eliminate the logarithms"
      ],
